# Exact-fingerprint suppressions for `gitleaks detect` (format: commit:path:rule:line).
#
# These are the ONLY suppressed findings. G19 deliberately performs no git-history rewrite, so the
# valueless Preview testnet wallet secret committed before it was untracked recurs on every
# full-history scan. Pinning fingerprints suppresses precisely those occurrences: a different
# secret, the same file at a different commit, or either field in the working tree still fails.
#
# Both lines of the historical file are listed because the custom `umbradb-wallet-seed-hex` rule
# catches BOTH the seed (line 4) and the derived night secret key (line 5). The stock
# undetected until that rule was added.
#
# The overlapping generic-api-key fingerprint was REMOVED: the custom rule takes precedence over
# it, so that entry was never consulted -- verified by deleting it and re-scanning clean.
#
# Verified: with these two entries, a full-history scan of 207 commits reports no leaks, while
# planting a fresh hex value in EITHER field of the tracked .example template fails the gate.
be646fcff58052a77e848914a79ccef2279cf78f:nix/midnight-env/test-wallets/preview-test-wallet.json:umbradb-wallet-seed-hex:4
